      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the ITE build fails because DEVICE_DEFINE as used by cros_flash_it8xxx2.c makes the device private so it can\u0027t be retrieved directly with DEVICE_DT_GET. I could either have flash.c continue to use device_get_binding() and retrieve the underlying device at runtime, or modify the ITE flash driver to make the device public.\n\nUsing device_get_binding() seems a little safer because its implementation checks that a device is correctly initialized before use, but then we retain the layer of indirection at runtime. Any opinion on which would be better?",
      "revId": "afa7e8ca54fa2433a93faf454962abe98da79f5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
